  "scope_and_overclaim_flags": [
    "Full-engine cases repeatedly reuse complete K3/K5/K7 graphs; eight-source case bypasses bounded signatures. No changing/sparse full-engine benchmark was run.",
    "Fresh GlobalState does not mean cold process caches. Warm memoized engine samples at n<=7 have 100% cache hits.",
    "Changing micro inputs repeat the same frozen 512-input sequence each pass. n3 has only eight distinct graphs and warms to 100% hits; n5/n7 retain 33.59375%/14.453125% hit fractions.",
    "Fixed-signature micro ratios (memoized/indexed about 38x-97x) are API hit-path results, not whole-engine or application speedups.",
    "Memoized n7 engine median is only 1.01386x and paired range crosses 1; n8 control ratios are near 1 with variation. Do not assert a robust general n7 gain.",
    "Collision controls have zero hits and 512 evictions per timed pass; memoized/indexed medians 0.97779x and 0.96989x indicate no miss-path advantage, with ranges crossing 1.",
    "Fresh-process memoized first-step medians are slower than indexed for n3/n5/n7 (ratios 0.85140/0.92014/0.93675).",
    "First-step intervals exclude process launch, input/config/GlobalState construction and serialization. They include lazy initialization inside macro_step and do not measure cold OS page-cache startup.",
    "Engine equality covers selected state fields plus complete crystals; micro equality covers complete canonical signature bytes for the frozen corpus. Neither is exhaustive correctness over all engine state/inputs.",
    "All three measured builds use Rust1.95.0 with LTO disabled as the recorded local linking workaround. Do not multiply ratios across comparisons or by historical ThinLTO measurements.",
    "Paired ranges quantify observed local variation; no statistical confidence intervals or general application/model performance claims are justified."
  ]
}
